== Effect ==
* Re-rolls obstacles in the current room into other random obstacles.
** {{Dlc|nr}} {{e|Poop}}s, {{E|TNT}}, {{e|Fire Place}}s and [[Key Block]]s cannot be re-rolled.
* Obstacles can reroll into: [[Rock]]s, [[Tinted rock]]s, [[Cobweb]]s, Chapter-specific obstacles ([[Urn]]s, [[Mushroom]]s, [[Skull]]s, and [[Polyp]]s), [[Metal Block]]s, Trap doors, {{r|Crawl Space}}s, {{E|TNT}}, {{E|White Poop}}, {{dlc+|r}} [[Fool's Gold]] Rocks, {{E|Reward Plate}}s and {{E|Killswitch}}es{{dlc-}}.
* {{dlc+|r}} Rerolled obstacles will only reroll into another one in this group: {{e|Poop}}s, [[Retractable Spikes]], Normal and Red {{e|Fire Place}}s, both types of {{E|TNT}}, and [[Cobweb]]s.
** Rerolled obstacles can also reroll into {{E|Reward Plate}}s and {{E|Killswitch}}es, but will not reroll any further. They can not roll into Trap doors or {{r|Crawl Space}}s. {{dlc-}}

== Notes ==
* Destroyed obstacles will not be rerolled.
* {{E|Rainbow Poop}}, {{E|Golden Poop}}, [[Tinted Rock]]s, Trap Doors, {{r|Crawl Space}}s, {{dlc|r}} [[Fool's Gold]] and {{E|Killswitch}}es are much less likely to be created by the D12 than all other obstacles.
* {{dlc|r}} It is possible to reroll the spikes in a {{R|Sacrifice Room}} and render the room unusable.
** Newly created spikes (but not retractable spikes) in {{r|Sacrifice Room}}s use separate reward counters, allowing you to get more rewards in one room.
* Each re-roll is seeded and will produce the same result for each room that the D12 is used in.

== Synergies ==
* {{t|Lucky Rock}}, {{t|Meconium}}, {{t|Petrified Poop}}, and {{t|Stud Finder}} can provide extra value in conjunction with their associated obstacles.
* {{i|Leo}} / {{i|Mega Mush}} / {{i|Notched Axe}} / {{i|Pyro}} / {{tf|Stompy}} / {{i|Sulfuric Acid}} / {{i|Terra}} / {{i|Thunder Thighs}} can provide Isaac a way to destroy the re-rolled obstacles.
* {{dlc|r}} {{i|Car Battery}}: Re-rolls have a higher chance of entering the looping pool and creating obstacles that can't reroll ({{E|Reward Plate}}s, {{E|Killswitch}}es, Trap doors and {{r|Crawl Space}}s)
* {{Book of Virtues synergy|description=Spawns blue die wisps on the middle ring. Wisps' tears have a 5% chance to reroll obstacles they hit. Poops, TNT barrels and metal blocks cannot be rerolled.}}
* {{dlc+|r}} {{p|XVI - The Tower?}} / {{p|A Card Against Humanity}}: Created obstacles can be rerolled into more useful objects such as {{E|Rainbow Poop}} or {{E|Golden Poop}}. Rocks created from {{p|XVI - The Tower?}} will have a larger pool to pick from. {{dlc-}}

== Interactions ==
* {{dlc|nr}} {{i|Car Battery}}: Re-rolls twice instantly without any benefits.

